age_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"Short answers to the questions that come up most."},"8":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"No. Everything the notebooks need runs from a cell or a card: `nb.kit_check()`, `nb.exakit(...)`, `nb.addon_ready(...)`. See Run the kit from a notebook."},"9":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"No. Every step runs without one. A model is used only to draft SQL in Ask and to sort texts into themes, and both are off until you turn them on. Ask also has a drafter with no model: `nb.draft_question`."},"10":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"Not by default. The database and the notebooks run on this computer. With a model set up, Ask sends the column map and your question, never rows. The themes step sends a sample of texts, and asks first when the data is a live external source."},"11":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"The column map: the role of every column in a table. See Descriptor and approval."},"12":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"You are. The kit proposes roles; a person approves them. A model never approves, and the kit never chooses the target."},"13":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"Explore, Ask and Share read only an approved column map. Open `00_quickstart`, review the map and approve it. See Review and approve the column map."},"14":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"Approve it in the quickstart. With `DATASET = None`, the other notebooks follow the dataset approved last when you run their first cell again. Or set `DATASET = \"...\"` in a notebook to pin one."},"15":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"Yes. Load a file with `nb.load_own_file(...)`, or use a table already in the database with `nb.use_table(...)`. See Load data."},"16":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"No. The checks only read. The joined view and the typed view are views in `EXAKIT_PREPARED`, created only when you ask."},"17":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"No. Nothing runs until you approve the exact text, and approved questions run as the read-only user."},"18":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"Under `~/.exasol-starter-kit`: column maps, workflow logs and hand-off bundles. See Where things live."},"19":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"No. A notebook you edited is never overwritten, and one you deleted is not copied back."},"20":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"Either. The same notebooks ship for both. `exakit notebook` opens JupyterLab and `exakit notebook marimo` opens Marimo."},"21":{"id":"/data-scientist/faq-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/faq","content":"`nb.docs(\"words\")` searches these docs, and `nb.docs(nb.some_command)` opens that command's page. All commands lists every one."},"22":{"id":"/data-scientist","page_id":"/data-scientist","type":"page","content":"Data Scientist notebooks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist"},"23":{"id":"/data-scientist-0","page_id":"/data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist","content":"What the Data Scientist persona gives you on your local Exasol database, and where to start."},"24":{"id":"/data-scientist-1","page_id":"/data-scientist","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist#these-docs-from-a-notebook","content":"These docs, from a notebook"},"25":{"id":"/data-scientist-2","page_id":"/data-scientist","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist#what-you-need","content":"What you need"},"26":{"id":"/data-scientist-3","page_id":"/data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist","content":"The Data Scientist persona gives you four notebooks that run on the Exasol database on this computer. They are one path with nine steps: get the data in, agree what each column means, prepare, explore, train and check a small model, ask questions in plain language, share a dashboard and hand the work off."},"27":{"id":"/data-scientist-4","page_id":"/data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist","content":"Every notebook opens with a **guided card** that does the page's steps with buttons and forms. Each card has a **Code** switch that shows the exact `exakit.nb` call behind every button, so anything you click you can also run in a cell."},"28":{"id":"/data-scientist-5","page_id":"/data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist#these-docs-from-a-notebook","content":"The site is a folder of files that ships with the kit. `nb.docs()` serves it from this computer only, so reading and searching work without internet."},"29":{"id":"/data-scientist-6","page_id":"/data-scientist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist#what-you-need","content":"Nothing beyond the kit. The persona installs the notebooks and their Python. An AI model is optional: every step except t