":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The table has not changed since it was profiled."},"190":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-73","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The data is checked again, and a column that gives the target away is reported."},"191":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-74","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The next **version** is written to the kit's store on this computer, under `~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/`."},"192":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-75","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The roles are published as column comments on a view in the `EXAKIT_SEMANTIC` schema. If publishing fails, the approval still stands and the message says why."},"193":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-76","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#what-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The active workflow's log gets one line."},"194":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-77","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#versions","content":"Every approval is a new version. Nothing is overwritten."},"195":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-78","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#versions","content":"Approving an older version's roles again brings it back as the newest version."},"196":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-79","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#reference","content":"`nb.describe`, `nb.Draft`, `nb.review_roles`, `nb.show_roles`, `nb.column_map_versions`, `nb.DescriptorNotApproved`."},"197":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"page","content":"Prepared views","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views"},"198":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","content":"Data checks, linked tables and the typed, cleaned view - how the data is prepared without ever changing your table."},"199":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#is-the-data-clean","content":"Is the data clean?"},"200":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"Linked tables"},"201":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#a-typed-cleaned-view","content":"A typed, cleaned view"},"202":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"Columns that give the answer away"},"203":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#reference","content":"Reference"},"204":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","content":"Step 3, Prepare, looks at the data before anything is computed from it. It never changes your table. What it creates, when you ask, are views in the `EXAKIT_PREPARED` schema."},"205":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#is-the-data-clean","content":"It looks for repeated keys, exact copies, gaps, placeholder values and a rare target. Each finding is one plain sentence that says what it does to a result. Deciding what to do about it is yours."},"206":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"The schema map shows the tables that link to this one, with the evidence for each link. A link adds the other table's columns without adding rows."},"207":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"To correct it: `schema_map.unlink(\"TABLE.COLUMN\")` or `schema_map.link(\"TABLE.COLUMN\", \"TABLE.KEY\")`."},"208":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"The **joined view** combines the table with every linked table. It is a proposal until you create it:"},"209":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#a-typed-cleaned-view","content":"It proposes correct types for numbers and dates stored as text, turns blanks and placeholders into NULL, and removes exact copies. Read what changes before you create it."},"210":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#a-typed-cleaned-view","content":"In `01_explore`, `USE_JOINED = True` and `USE_PREPARED = True` in the first cell create these views and make the later steps read them."},"211":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"A column whose values almost decide the target on their own would make a model look better than it is. These columns are listed and left out of the model."},"212":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#reference","content":"Data checks, Schema map and joined view, Typed view."},"213":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"page","content":"Sharing and hand-off","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff"},"214":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","content":"A dashboard that goes up as a preview first, and one folder that lets a colleague repeat the work."},"215":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"A dashboard, preview first"},"216":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The hand-off bundle"},"217":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-training-handoff","content":"The training handoff"},"218":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#reference","content":"Reference"},"219":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"Step 8 turns one checked result into a dashboard others open in a browser. Dashboards run on **Dash Server**, a kit add-on the notebook installs and starts for you."},"220":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"`nb.share(...)` prepares a dashboard from approved roles and SQL you can read."},"221":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"It goes up as a **preview**. You open it and check that the figures match the query."},"222":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"Only then is it **published**: `dashboard_draft.confirm(dash_server, figures_checked=True)`."},"223":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"A preview that was not checked is never promoted. In automated runs the check is never set, so nothing is published without a person."},"224":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"Step 9 packs the work into one folder and a zip."},"225":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"It is written to `~/.exasol-starter-kit/bundles/<workflow id>/` and holds:"},"226":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"File"},"227":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"What it is"},"228":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`descriptor.yaml`"},"229":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The approved column map"},"230":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`schema-map.json`"},"231":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The schema map, when there is one"},"232":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`queries.sql`"},"233":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"Every query the workflow ran, with its digest and row count"},"234":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`workflow.jsonl`"},"235":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The workflow log as it is"},"236":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`README.md`"},"237":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"What the data is, which column map version the numbers rest on, what was approved and published, and how to repeat it"},"238":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"Nothing in it is a password."},"239":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-training-handoff","content":"The ML Engineer's handoff is a different thing: one JSON file with the feature view, the target and a reproducible split, written by `nb.write_handoff(connection, dataset)` to `~/.exasol-starter-kit/handoffs/`. A stale one is refused, and `nb.handoff_is_stale` names what changed."},"240":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#reference","content":"Share a dashboard, Dash Server tools, Hand-off bundle, Training handoff."},"241":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"page","content":"Sources","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources"},"242":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","content":"The three ways data comes in, and how an external source appears as a schema in your local database."},"243":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-kit-dataset","content":"A kit dataset"},"244":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#your-own-data","content":"Your own data"},"245":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#an-external-source","content":"An external source"},"246":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"A source with several kinds in one"},"247":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#one-source-engine","content":"One source engine"},"248":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"Passwords"},"249":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#live-sources-and-ai","content":"Live sources and AI"},"250":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#reference","content":"Reference"},"251":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","content":"Data reaches the notebooks in three ways. All three end the same way: a table or view the kit can describe, and a column map you approve."},"252":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-kit-dataset","content":"Practice data that ships with the kit, such as `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions`. `nb.sample_datasets()` lists them and says which are loaded."},"253":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#your-own-data","content":"A CSV, Parquet, JSON or Excel file, a folder of them, or a table already in the database. Files are loaded with the kit's own loader, the one `exakit data-load` runs."},"254":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#an-external-source","content":"A database or lake elsewhere: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Snowflake and others. The kit connects it as a **virtual schema**: its tables appear in your local Exasol as `VS_<NAME>` and are read from the source when you query them. Nothing is copied."},"255":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"A **Lakehouse** is one connector for several things: an Iceberg REST catalog, Unity Catalog, AWS Glue, or Parquet files in a plain folder, with the files on S3 or Azure. Two **settings** pick the combination, and each combination asks for different details."},"256":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"In the **Data source** list it appears as a tree, the same one the terminal's connect menu shows:"},"257":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"Pick a **leaf** and both settings are chosen."},"258":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"A setting the tree does not hold, such as the catalog login (token or OAuth), is asked in one more step."},"259":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"Pick **Lakehouse** itself and the settings are asked one by one."},"260":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"In code the settings are plain inputs:"},"261":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"Some combinations have **two secrets**: the catalog login and the storage keys. The login is asked like any password. The storage secret travels in a file only you can read, removed as soon as the kit has read it."},"262":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#one-source-engine","content":"The connectors, their inputs and the connection-string reader come from the kit's source engine, the one `exakit connect` runs. Nothing about a connector is defined in the notebooks, so a connector added to the kit appears in the form with no notebook change."},"263":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"A password is asked in a hidden box and handed to `exakit connect` on standard input."},"264":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"It is never written into a cell, the code view or the workflow log."},"265":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"A password inside a connection string is used and never shown."},"266":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"A second secret (a Lakehouse's storage keys) goes to the kit in a private file, never on a command line."},"267":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#live-sources-and-ai","content":"A table from an external source is read from there as you query it. Before sampled rows from a live source go to a model, the notebook names the source and asks. Only a yes sends them."},"268":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#reference","content":"External sources, Your own file or table, Data map."},"269":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"page","content":"Workflow","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow"},"270":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","content":"One id on everything a piece of work does, and the log it leaves."},"271":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#what-is-logged","content":"What is logged"},"272":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#where-the-log-is","content":"Where the log is"},"273":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#no-secrets-in-the-log","content":"No secrets in the log"},"274":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#reference","content":"Reference"},"275":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","content":"A **workflow** gives one id to every query and decision in a piece of work. The quickstart starts it and the other notebooks continue it. You never paste an id."},"276":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","content":"`continue_workflow` takes this kernel's workflow, else the last one started on this computer, and starts a new one only when there is none."},"277":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#what-is-logged","content":"While a workflow is active, every helper that does something appends one line to its log: a SQL statement, a column map draft or approval, a model trace, a dashboard revision, a hand-off. Every guided card action is a line too, with the code it ran and whether it worked."},"278":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#what-is-logged","content":"Without a workflow nothing is written. There are no implicit workflows."},"279":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#where-the-log-is","content":"`~/.exasol-starter-kit/workflows/<id>.jsonl`: one JSON object per line, append-only, readable by you only. The id looks like `wf-20261027-3f9a1c`."},"280":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#no-secrets-in-the-log","content":"A secret-named value or a connection string with a password is refused before anything is written. SQL that mentions a password or an API key is logged with its text replaced and its digest kept."},"281":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#no-secrets-in-the-log","content":"A log that cannot be written warns and the cell goes on. Logging never fails the work it describes."},"282":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#reference","content":"Workflows."},"283":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"page","content":"Review and approve the column map","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map"},"284":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","content":"Check the roles the kit proposed, correct them, choose the target and approve."},"285":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#open-the-review","content":"Open the review"},"286":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#check-the-uncertain-columns-first","content":"Check the uncertain columns first"},"287":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#correct-roles-and-choose-the-target","content":"Correct roles and choose the target"},"288":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#approve","content":"Approve"},"289":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#read-it-back","content":"Read it back"},"290":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#after-approving","content":"After approving"},"291":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#change-your-mind-later","content":"Change your mind later"},"292":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","content":"This is step 2 of `00_quickstart`. Until the map is approved, Explore, Ask and Share have nothing to read. For what the roles and slots mean, see Descriptor and approval."},"293":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#open-the-review","content":"The kit profiles the table and proposes a role for every column."},"294":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#check-the-uncertain-columns-first","content":"**Check these first** lists the columns the kit was least sure about, each with the evidence that chose its role. Start there."},"295":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#correct-roles-and-choose-the-target","content":"Change a role where it is wrong. Choose the **target**: the outcome you want to predict. The kit never chooses it. Leave a slot empty when no column fits."},"296":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#approve","content":"Press **Approve column map**, or in code:"},"297":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#approve","content":"The first argument is the roles you change, the second the slots. With nothing to change, the saved approval stands."},"298":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#after-approving","content":"Approval checks the data again. A warning about a column that gives the target away is not an error: the column stays in the map and is left out of the model."},"299":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#change-your-mind-later","content":"Open the quickstart, change the roles and approve again. That writes a new version. The other notebooks follow the newest approval when you run their first cell again."},"300":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","type":"page","content":"Ask your data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask"},"301":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","content":"Ask in plain language, read the proposed SQL, approve it and run it read-only."},"302":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#ask","content":"Ask"},"303":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#get-a-proposal","content":"Get a proposal"},"304":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#read-it-and-edit-if-needed","content":"Read it, and edit if needed"},"305":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#approve-and-run","content":"Approve and run"},"306":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","content":"This is step 7, in `02_ask_your_data`."},"307":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#get-a-proposal","content":"Three ways to draft the SQL:"},"308":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#get-a-proposal","content":"With a model, only the approved column map and the question are sent. No rows."},"309":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#read-it-and-edit-if-needed","content":"A proposed query can be wrong: a wrong column, a missing filter. Read it."},"310":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#approve-and-run","content":"Only the exact approved text runs, through the kit's read-only service as the read-only user. Check the figures against the SQL."},"311":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#approve-and-run","content":"Nothing runs before `approve()`. In the notebook, set `APPROVE_SQL = True` and run the cell again."},"312":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#approve-and-run","content":"See AI and tracing and Set up a model."},"313":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"page","content":"Explore and model","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model"},"314":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","content":"Steps 3 to 6 in 01_explore - prepare the data, compare groups, train a baseline model and check it."},"315":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#prepare","content":"Prepare"},"316":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#explore","content":"Explore"},"317":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"Model and validate"},"318":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","content":"`01_explore` reads the dataset you approved. Its first cell holds the choices:"},"319":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#prepare","content":"Read the findings and the two proposals. Nothing is created until you set `USE_JOINED` or `USE_PREPARED`. See Prepared views."},"320":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#explore","content":"Each query shows its SQL before its result, and a plain-language note under it."},"321":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#explore","content":"`nb.note_groups` and `nb.note_trend` write the notes under the group and over-time results."},"322":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"The notebook then reads up to 20,000 rows, trains a small baseline model on the category, the entity and the month, scores it on rows it has not seen, and shows what it leans on. `nb.note_model` says in plain words what the score means."},"323":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"For more control, the **model lab** lets you choose the task, the model and the split:"},"324":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"See Model lab."},"325":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"A dataset with no target skips the model steps and says so. Choose a target in the column map to run them."},"326":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","type":"page","content":"Load data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data"},"327":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"Three ways to get data in front of the notebooks - a kit dataset, your own file or table, or an external source."},"328":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#use-what-you-chose","content":"Use what you chose"},"329":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"All of this happens in step 1 of `00_quickstart`. On the **Choose your data** card you pick one of three boxes. The code below is what each box runs."},"330":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A dataset that is not loaded yet is loaded first. Nothing else is needed."},"331":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A file or a folder:"},"332":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"CSV, Parquet, JSON and Excel work. Leave the schema empty and it is named after the folder: `~/sales-data` becomes `SALES_DATA`."},"333":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A table that is already in the database:"},"334":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"`nb.data_map(connection)` lists every table the database holds."},"335":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"The card walks through it one step at a time: an existing connection or a new one, the kind of source, a connection string or manual details, a name, the password, and optional settings."},"336":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A source with several kinds in one, such as a Lakehouse, shows its choices as a tree under it in the **Data source** list. Pick the catalog and where its files are; the steps after it ask only what that combination needs. See Sources."},"337":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"**Test connection** checks the inputs and reaches the source from this computer. It changes nothing."},"338":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"**Connect and use this data** runs `exakit connect`. The tables then appear as `VS_SALES`."},"339":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"The password is asked in a hidden box. It is never part of the code."},"340":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#use-what-you-chose","content":"Next: approve the column map."},"341":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#use-what-you-chose","content":"A source on this computer is not `localhost` from the database's point of view. On macOS use `192.168.64.1`. For a cloud source, allow this computer's public IP there; the card shows it."},"342":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","type":"page","content":"Run the kit from a notebook","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit"},"343":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","content":"Check, update and extend the kit without leaving the notebook."},"344":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit#see-what-is-there","content":"See what is there"},"345":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit#change-it","content":"Change it"},"346":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit#reference","content":"Reference"},"347":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","content":"Step 0 of the quickstart is the kit itself. Every command here is the same `exakit` a terminal runs, with its output streaming into the cell."},"348":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit#change-it","content":"`nb.exakit(...)` returns the run with its exit code, so a cell can act on it."},"349":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit#change-it","content":"A command run from a cell has no terminal, so a question it would ask takes its default. Give a choice up front instead: `nb.exakit(\"mcp-setup\", env={\"EXAKIT_MCP_CLIENTS\": \"claude\"})`."},"350":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit#reference","content":"Kit commands, Kit facts."},"351":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","type":"page","content":"Set up a model","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model"},"352":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","content":"Point the notebooks at your AI model and, optionally, at Langfuse for tracing."},"353":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-quickest-way","content":"The quickest way"},"354":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#in-a-cell","content":"In a cell"},"355":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#check-and-forget","content":"Check and forget"},"356":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"The settings behind it"},"357":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","content":"A model is optional. It is used to draft SQL in Ask and to sort texts into themes in Explore. Any endpoint that speaks the Chat Completions API works: an external provider or a model on your own machine."},"358":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-quickest-way","content":"It asks for anything missing, with the keys in a hidden box, says what is set, and prints the lines that set the same thing for every notebook."},"359":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#in-a-cell","content":"The API key is asked in a hidden box. With `remember=True` it is kept in the kit's credentials, readable by you only."},"360":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"Setting"},"361":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"What it is"},"362":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"`EXAKIT_MODEL_ID`"},"363":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"The model's id"},"364":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"`EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL`"},"365":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"The endpoint's address"},"366":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"`EXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY`"},"367":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"The key"},"368":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"`LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY`, `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY`, `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL`"},"369":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"Turn tracing on"},"370":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"The model's id and address can also live in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/exakit.env`. Provider recipes are in `MODEL-PROVIDERS.md`, copied beside the notebooks."},"371":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/set-up-a-model#the-settings-behind-it","content":"Never type a key into a cell. Use the hidden box, so the key is not saved in the notebook file."},"372":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","type":"page","content":"Share a dashboard and hand off","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/share"},"373":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/share","content":"Steps 8 and 9 in 03_share - a dashboard that is previewed, checked and published, then one folder to hand the work on."},"374":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#prepare-the-dashboard","content":"Prepare the dashboard"},"375":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#start-dash-server","content":"Start Dash Server"},"376":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#preview","content":"Preview"},"377":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#publish","content":"Publish"},"378":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#hand-off","content":"Hand off"},"379":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#prepare-the-dashboard","content":"The dashboard is built from approved roles and a query you can read."},"380":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#start-dash-server","content":"It installs Dash Server when it is missing and starts it when it is stopped. This is what `exakit marketplace dash-server` and `exakit start dash-server` do."},"381":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#preview","content":"Open it. Check that the categories and counts match your SQL, and that the filters update both charts and the table."},"382":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#publish","content":"Set `figures_checked=True` only when the preview matches the query. Keep the live address with your workflow id."},"383":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/share-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/share#hand-off","content":"One folder and a zip under `~/.exasol-starter-kit/bundles/`. It needs no Dash Server and holds no password. See Sharing and hand-off."},"384":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","type":"page","content":"Add a command","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","For developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command"},"385":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","content":"Add an exakit.nb helper, wire it to a card, and get its documentation for free."},"386":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#write-the-helper","content":"Write the helper"},"387":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#put-it-in-a-notebook","content":"Put it in a notebook"},"388":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#give-a-card-a-button-for-it","content":"Give a card a button for it"},"389":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#regenerate","content":"Regenerate"},"390":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#test","content":"Test"},"391":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#write-the-helper","content":"Add a function to a module in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/`, with a docstring. The first sentence becomes its one-line summary here; the rest becomes its reference text. Indented lines in a docstring are shown as code."},"392":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#write-the-helper","content":"Export it: import it in `exakit_nb/__init__.py` and add its name to `__all__`."},"393":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#put-it-in-a-notebook","content":"Add the call to the code section of the notebook it belongs to, guarded by a variable when it is optional:"},"394":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#give-a-card-a-button-for-it","content":"Add one entry to `actions.ACTIONS` in `exakit_guide/actions.py`: the code and the notebook it belongs to. Have the screen call `actions.run(...)`."},"395":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#regenerate","content":"The new helper now has an entry in its module's reference page and a row in All commands. `nb.docs(nb.your_helper)` opens it once the site is rebuilt."},"396":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#test","content":"A whole new module gets its own reference page automatically, titled from its file name. Give it a proper title and a place in the order by adding one line to `PAGES` in `tools/nb_docs.py`."},"397":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"page","content":"These docs","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","For developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site"},"398":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","content":"How this documentation is written, built and shipped, and how to change a page."},"399":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"400":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#change-a-page","content":"Change a page"},"401":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#edit","content":"Edit"},"402":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#preview-while-you-write","content":"Preview while you write"},"403":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#build-and-publish","content":"Build and publish"},"404":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#check","content":"Check"},"405":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#pages-you-do-not-edit","content":"Pages you do not edit"},"406":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#links","content":"Links"},"407":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Source:** MDX pages in `notebook/docs/content/docs/`, one folder per persona. The folder layout is the sidebar; each folder's `meta.json` sets its title and page order, and a persona's folder is marked `\"root\": true`, which makes it an entry in the list at the top of the sidebar."},"408":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Build:** a static site built with Node on a maintainer's machine. Users never need Node."},"409":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Shipped:** the built files, in `notebook/docs/site/`, travel with the kit."},"410":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Served:** `nb.docs()` serves that folder from the kit's own Python, on this computer only."},"411":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"Search runs in the browser on an index inside the site. It forgives typos, matches as you type and needs no internet."},"412":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#edit","content":"Edit an `.mdx` file, or add one and list it in its folder's `meta.json`. Each page starts with:"},"413":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#edit","content":"`Callout`, `Tabs`, `Steps`, `Cards` and `Accordions` are available on every page without imports."},"414":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#preview-while-you-write","content":"Run both in `notebook/docs`. The site is at `http://localhost:3000/docs` and reloads on every save."},"415":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#build-and-publish","content":"The first writes `notebook/docs/out`; the second copies it to `notebook/docs/site` and stamps it with a digest of the sources."},"416":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#check","content":"It fails when a generated page is stale, or when the shipped site was built from older sources than the ones in the repository."},"417":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#pages-you-do-not-edit","content":"Everything under a persona's `reference/` folder is generated from the docstrings in `exakit_nb` by `python3 tools/nb_docs.py`. To change a command's text, change its docstring and run the tool."},"418":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#links","content":"Link to a page by its address, without the `/docs` prefix and without `.mdx`: `/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor`. Link to a command by its page and name: `/data-scientist/reference/describe#describe`. A test fails on a link that leads nowhere."},"419":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"page","content":"How it fits together","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","For developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits"},"420":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","content":"The helpers, the guided cards and the kit - which part owns what, and the rules that keep them honest."},"421":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Three layers"},"422":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"The helpers"},"423":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-guided-view","content":"The guided view"},"424":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"Rules the tests enforce"},"425":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#notebooks","content":"Notebooks"},"426":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Layer"},"427":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Where"},"428":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"What it owns"},"429":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The kit"},"430":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"`setup/`, the `exakit` command"},"431":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The database, connections, loading, connectors, add-ons, the describe service"},"432":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The helpers"},"433":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"`notebook/package/exakit_nb/` (`import exakit.nb as nb`)"},"434":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"One Python call for each thing a notebook does"},"435":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The guided view"},"436":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"`notebook/package/exakit_guide/` (`exakit.guide`)"},"437":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Cards that call the helpers; UI only"},"438":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"A notebook is cells that call the helpers. A card is a form that calls the same helpers. Neither talks to the database on its own."},"439":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"`exakit.nb` exports about 110 names, listed in All commands. The rules they follow:"},"440":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**The connection comes from the kit.** `nb.connect()` opens it from the kit's encrypted store. No helper prints or returns a host, a user or a password."},"441":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**The kit does the work.** Describing a table is the kit's describe service; loading is `exakit data-load`; connecting a source is `exakit connect`. The helpers call these, they do not reimplement them."},"442":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**SQL is shown.** `nb.sql` records the statement, `nb.show_sql()` prints it, and the workflow logs it."},"443":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**Reads are live.** `nb.components()`, `nb.addons()`, `nb.connectors()` and the rest ask the kit when called."},"444":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-guided-view","content":"`actions.code(id, **values)` is the exact cell text. `actions.run(id, **values)` runs that text in the notebook's namespace and logs it. A screen changes nothing except through `actions.run`, which is why **Code** can always show what a card did."},"445":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"An action's call exists in its notebook's code section, and calls something `exakit.nb` exports."},"446":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"No screen names a dataset, connector, add-on or notebook. Those are read from the kit."},"447":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"No action shows a secret: a key is bound at run time, never written into the code."},"448":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"Every exported helper has a page in these docs, and every link in them leads somewhere."},"449":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#notebooks","content":"Sources are `notebook/notebooks/<persona>/<NN>_<name>.py` in jupytext percent format. The `.ipynb` and the Marimo version are built from them:"},"450":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live","page_id":