ur data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask"},"492":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","content":"Ask a question, inspect the proposed SQL, approve that exact text, then run through the Exasol MCP server."},"493":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#ask","content":"nb.ask"},"494":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"nb.Proposal"},"495":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","content":"The archived Governed SQL server is not installed. The kit's own model endpoint can draft SQL from an approved\ndescriptor; no SQL runs until the person approves it. The SQL runs on the launcher's MCP server beside the\ndatabase (the sidecar, on loopback), which connects as the dedicated read-only user only - never the notebook's\nadmin connection or an admin fallback. The notebook sends no password: the sidecar holds the read-only login."},"496":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#ask","content":"Draft SQL from roles and the user's opted-in model endpoint; `proposed_sql` supports manual drafting."},"497":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#ask","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"498":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"A question with the SQL proposed for it. Nothing runs until `approve()` accepts that exact text; `edit()` replaces\nthe SQL and removes the approval; `run()` runs the approved text through the kit's read-only service."},"499":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"Member"},"500":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"What it is"},"501":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`dataset`"},"502":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`Any`"},"503":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`question`"},"504":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`str`"},"505":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`sql`"},"506":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`str`"},"507":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`assumptions`"},"508":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`list[str]`"},"509":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`doubts`"},"510":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`list[str]`"},"511":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`edit(sql: str) -> Proposal`"},"512":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`approve() -> Proposal`"},"513":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ask#Proposal","content":"`run()`"},"514":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","type":"page","content":"ML Engineer checks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks"},"515":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","content":"The three things the ML Engineer's notebooks depend on, one check each (ml-engineer/00_quickstart): the database's Python container answers a smoke UDF with the packages training needs, the MLflow server is reachable, and the bucket directory is where the kit expects it."},"516":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_bucket","content":"nb.check_bucket"},"517":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_container","content":"nb.check_container"},"518":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_mlflow","content":"nb.check_mlflow"},"519":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_model_compatibility","content":"nb.check_model_compatibility"},"520":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#model_list","content":"nb.model_list"},"521":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","content":"The three things the ML Engineer's notebooks depend on, one check each (ml-engineer/00_quickstart): the database's\nPython container answers a smoke UDF with the packages training needs, the MLflow server is reachable, and the bucket\ndirectory is where the kit expects it. Each prints one line - `ok` with what it found, or `FAIL` with the reason\nand the fix - and returns True or False, so the notebook shows all three before anything stops."},"522":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","content":"Nothing here prints a host, a user or a password; an MLflow address is shown without any credentials it holds."},"523":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_bucket","content":"The deployment's bucket directory exists on this machine where the kit says it is, and - given a connection -\na UDF sees it at its /buckets path too (skipped, with a note, when the container check fails)."},"524":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_bucket","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"525":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_container","content":"The container behind `alias` runs a smoke UDF, and it has every package training needs. The line names the\nalias probed and the fix for that alias (PYTHON3_ML: exakit udf-use default; PYTHON3: exakit udf-setup), so the\nfix installs the container the check looks at. `alias` None is the notebook's default, ml_train.udf_container():\nPYTHON3_ML before PYTHON3 from the kit's manifest, EXAKIT_UDF_CONTAINER first; none installed is a FAIL line."},"526":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_container","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"527":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_mlflow","content":"Check the destination runs will really use: configured server, kit server, or local store."},"528":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_mlflow","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"529":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_model_compatibility","content":"Refuse a pickle whose scikit-learn version differs before any scoring SQL runs."},"530":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#check_model_compatibility","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"531":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/checks#model_list","content":"What `exakit model list --json` says: bucket_dir (the host folder), udf_root (the path UDFs read it under) and\nthe models in it. Raises RuntimeError naming why it could not be read."},"532":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"page","content":"Connect, SQL and tracing","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core"},"533":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core","content":"Helpers for the Exasol Personal Local Starter Kit's notebooks: exakit.nb (this module; exakit_nb is the same module under its older name)."},"534":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#confirm_send","content":"nb.confirm_send"},"535":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#connect","content":"nb.connect"},"536":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#model_client","content":"nb.model_client"},"537":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#model_settings","content":"nb.model_settings"},"538":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#show_sql","content":"nb.show_sql"},"539":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#sql","content":"nb.sql"},"540":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#trace","content":"nb.trace"},"541":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#tracing","content":"nb.tracing"},"542":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core","content":"The connection comes from the kit. Its Jupyter kernel (\"Exasol (Starter Kit)\") carries two paths: the encrypted\nconfiguration store, and the kit's credential file holding the store's master password, readable by the user only.\nThese helpers open the database from there, in JupyterLab, Marimo, VS Code or any front end that runs the\nkit's notebook Python. Nothing here prints or returns a host, a user or a password."},"543":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core","content":"The quickstarts' shared steps (check_connection, list_schemas, load_sample, load_source, ...) are in quickstart.py;\nthe ML Engineer's checks (check_container, check_mlflow, check_bucket) in checks.py."},"544":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#confirm_send","content":"Before sampled rows go to a model endpoint: True at once for a table in the database; for a live source (the\ndescriptor names a source) it names the source and asks, and only a yes sends. `answer` answers for a script;\nwith no one to ask (a headless run) the answer is no."},"545":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#confirm_send","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"546":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#connect","content":"A pyexasol connection to the local database, opened from the kit's encrypted store, pinned to the database's\nTLS certificate once the kit has recorded it. Exasol's usage telemetry stays off unless EXASOL_TELEMETRY_DISABLE\nwas already set."},"547":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#connect","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/01_train`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`, `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"548":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#model_client","content":"(client, model ID) for EXAKIT_MODEL_ID and EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL; EXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY is optional for\nservers without authentication. Tracing uses Langfuse's instrumented client for the same endpoint and key.\nThis interface makes text Chat Completions calls; it does not provide a provider's native API features."},"549":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#model_client","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"550":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#model_settings","content":"Display the chosen model and endpoint without the API key or custom header values; makes no request."},"551":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#model_settings","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"552":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#show_sql","content":"Print the last statement sql() ran, so a result can always be traced to the query behind it."},"553":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#show_sql","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"554":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#sql","content":"Run a query and return its rows as a pandas DataFrame; the statement is remembered for show_sql()."},"555":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#sql","content":"The rows come over the normal connection rather than pyexasol's HTTP export, which needs the database to connect\nback to this machine - not a given through the local VM or Podman."},"556":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#sql","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`, `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"557":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#trace","content":"Group the model calls made inside the block into one trace in the user's own Langfuse project, tagged with the\ndatabase session, the sample SQL, the workflow id and, given a dataset, its id, descriptor digest and descriptor\nversion (trace_tags). Opt-in: without LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY, LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY and LANGFUSE_BASE_URL (LANGFUSE_HOST,\nthe SDK 3/4 name, still counts) it says so in one line and does nothing else - no exception, no prompt."},"558":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#trace","content":"Langfuse SDK 5: the block is one observation (`Langfuse.start_as_current_observation`) and, right inside it, the\ntrace name, session id, tags and metadata are propagated (`langfuse.propagate_attributes`, a module function in\nSDK 5) to it and to every observation opened within, so each call the client model_client() returns makes -\nLangfuse's OpenAI drop-in when tracing is on - lands in this one trace with its input, output, token usage and\nlatency, without changes to the calling code. The span is yielded; the client is flushed when the block ends.\nThe active workflow's log gets one `trace` line with the trace id (X-1), and when the block ends one line is\nprinted - `traced: <trace id> (<url or base URL>)` - so the trace can be found in Langfuse. Nothing here prints\nor records the secret key."},"559":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#tracing","content":"Whether LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY, LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY and LANGFUSE_BASE_URL (or LANGFUSE_HOST) are all set, so trace()\nrecords to the user's Langfuse."},"560":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/core-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/core#tracing","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"561":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","type":"page","content":"Dash Server tools","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp"},"562":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","content":"Call the kit-managed Dash Server through its MCP control plane."},"563":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp#dash_tools","content":"nb.dash_tools"},"564":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp#DashTools","content":"nb.DashTools"},"565":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp#dash_tools","content":"The notebook's Dash Server tool adapter; each call is an MCP tool call."},"566":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp#dash_tools","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/03_share`"},"567":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dash-mcp#DashTools","content":"Synchronous adapter for notebook cells, which already run an event loop."},"568":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","type":"page","content":"Data checks","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks"},"569":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","content":"Prepare and Validate: what the data itself says is wrong with it, and any column that gives the label away."},"570":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks#data_checks","content":"nb.data_checks"},"571":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks#leakage_check","content":"nb.leakage_check"},"572":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","content":"Both are built from the descriptor alone - the key, the label and every column's role - so no column name is typed in\na notebook and the same cell runs on every dataset. Each check is one or two SQL statements, run through nb.sql (so\nthey are shown and logged like every other query), and each finding is one plain sentence saying what it does to a\nresult. Nothing is changed in the data: deciding what to do about a finding is the user's."},"573":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks#data_checks","content":"Prepare: one row per finding - CHECK, COLUMN_NAME, ROWS_AFFECTED, PCT, MEANS - for repeated keys, repeated\nidentifiers, exact copies of a row, empty cells, placeholder values and a rare label. Prints each finding in one\nsentence (`show=False` only returns them); an empty frame means the table passed every check."},"574":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks#data_checks","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"575":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks#leakage_check","content":"Validate: the columns whose values (almost) decide the label on their own - each a value or values where the\nlabel is (nearly) always 1 or always 0, covering most rows. Such a column is usually written after the outcome\n(an order's status once it was cancelled) and makes any model look perfect; leave it out of the features. Returns\nthose columns (none: the list is empty) and prints why each was flagged."},"576":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-checks#leakage_check","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"577":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","type":"page","content":"Data map","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map"},"578":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","content":"One semantic map of everything the database holds, wherever it came from."},"579":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#data_map","content":"nb.data_map"},"580":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"nb.DataMap"},"581":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","content":"Three origins, one view:"},"582":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","content":"\\*\\*sample\\*\\*: a dataset the kit ships (`exakit data-load amazon_sales`);"},"583":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","content":"\\*\\*local\\*\\*: your own file or folder (`exakit data-load <path>`, the quickstart's MY_DATA cell);"},"584":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","content":"\\*\\*source\\*\\*: a connected external source, read live through its virtual schema (`exakit connect`)."},"585":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","content":"Roles come from the approved column maps (EXAKIT_SEMANTIC.\\<SCHEMA>\\_\\_\\<TABLE>, one column comment per role) and the\nlinks from approved schema maps (EXAKIT_SEMANTIC.\\<SCHEMA>\\_\\_RELATIONS). Columns that share a key-like name across\ntwo tables are listed as possible links: a lead to check, never a join made for you. Only metadata is read."},"586":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#data_map","content":"The semantic map of the database: every table by origin (sample, local, source) with its rows, columns,\ncolumn-map state and roles, then the links between tables - declared, found by an approved schema map, or a\nshared key-like column name across two tables (marked possible). Reads metadata only; returns a DataMap that\nshows itself as a table in a notebook. `include_kit` keeps the kit's own schemas in."},"587":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"What data_map found: tables, columns and links, each a list of dicts; DataFrames through the properties."},"588":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"Member"},"589":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"What it is"},"590":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`table_rows`"},"591":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`list[dict[str, Any]]`"},"592":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`column_rows`"},"593":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`list[dict[str, Any]]`"},"594":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`link_rows`"},"595":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`list[dict[str, Any]]`"},"596":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`tables`"},"597":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`columns`"},"598":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`links`"},"599":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`table(name: str) -> dict[str, Any]`"},"600":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"One table's row, by SCHEMA.TABLE (any case)."},"601":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"`roles(name: str) -> dict[str, str]`"},"602":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/data-map#DataMap","content":"\\{column: role} of one table's approved column map; empty when it has none yet."},"603":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","type":"page","content":"Datasets","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset"},"604":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","content":"A dataset the notebooks run on: its descriptor read, validated by the kit's own rules, held against the database, and the roles turned into SQL names, so one notebook runs unchanged on any dataset whose descriptor is valid."},"605":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#chosen_dataset","content":"nb.chosen_dataset"},"606":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"nb.Dataset"},"607":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#dataset","content":"nb.dataset"},"608":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#DescriptorNotApproved","content":"nb.DescriptorNotApproved"},"609":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","content":"The rules are the kit's descriptor rules (`descriptor_rules`, shipped with this package: the 0.2 kit has no Python\npackage to import them from). It is a copy of tools/descriptor_rules.py, which tools/dataset_check.py uses, and\ntests/test_notebook_contents.py holds the two byte-identical. Nothing is guessed: a descriptor that is invalid, or\nnames a table or column the database lacks, stops the notebook with the reason."},"610":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","content":"Which descriptor a name resolves to, in order: a path given (a file, or a folder holding descriptor.yaml); for a\ndata file of your own, `<name>.descriptor.yaml` beside it; for an id, the approved version in the kit's store\n(`~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/<SCHEMA>.<TABLE>/current.yaml`, or an older kit's `descriptors/<id>/current`;\ndescriptor_store), then the descriptor the kit ships under\n`data/datasets/<id>/`. `ds.descriptor_path` and `ds.descriptor_origin` say which one was used."},"611":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#chosen_dataset","content":"The dataset a notebook works on: `name` when it is set; with None, the one approved last in a quickstart (so\npicking fraud_transactions there carries on here), else amazon_sales. Says which, and why, in one line."},"612":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#chosen_dataset","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/01_train`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`, `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"613":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"A validated descriptor whose every role the database holds, with the SQL names the notebooks build queries from."},"614":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"Member"},"615":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"What it is"},"616":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`id`"},"617":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`str`"},"618":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`path`"},"619":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`Path`"},"620":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`digest`"},"621":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`str`"},"622":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`descriptor`"},"623":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`Any`"},"624":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`descriptor_path`"},"625":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"\\`Path"},"626":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"None\\`"},"627":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`descriptor_origin`"},"628":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text