up, and counting by that target is its overview."},"669":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-65","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"`tags() -> dict[str, str]`"},"670":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-66","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#Dataset","content":"What a trace or an MLflow run records about the data: the dataset and the descriptor's digest (and the source's alias for a live source)."},"671":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-67","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#dataset","content":"The dataset `name`, checked against the database: a kit dataset id, a descriptor file or its folder, or a data\nfile of your own (CSV, Parquet or JSON) with its descriptor beside it, which is loaded first (load_own_file)."},"672":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-68","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#dataset","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/01_train`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`, `ml-engineer/03_score_external_model`"},"673":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset-69","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/dataset#DescriptorNotApproved","content":"A step that needs an approved descriptor was given a draft; the message says how to approve it."},"674":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","type":"page","content":"Describe a table","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe"},"675":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","content":"Describe a table from a notebook (DS-2, DS-5): the role-per-column descriptor of setup/lib/descriptor."},"676":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#describe","content":"nb.describe"},"677":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#Draft","content":"nb.Draft"},"678":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","content":"describe() on a table whose approved descriptor still matches it returns that one (force=True profiles again);\notherwise the table is profiled once, in SQL, and every column gets one of eight roles with the evidence that chose\nit; the slots name the columns the notebooks use. show() lists each column with the schema and table it came from,\nits type, role, confidence, evidence and note, low confidence first, the slots above (rows() gives the same as dicts;\na notebook renders it as a table). approve() checks every column has a role and none sits in two slots, checks\nthe table has not changed since it was profiled, writes the next version into the kit's store and publishes the\nroles as column comments on a view in EXAKIT_SEMANTIC (a publish that fails leaves the approval standing, and says\nwhy). The active workflow's log gets one line."},"679":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","content":"The work is the kit's own service, setup/lib/describe_service.py in the kit copy (the one `exakit describe` runs),\nloaded from its file and run in this process over the kit's connection; without the kit copy, `exakit describe --json` runs as a child process instead."},"680":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","content":"The role review (role_picker) speaks the five roles of earlier descriptors - entity, category, date, label, text - so\n`roles`, `evidence`, `missing` and `set(role, column)` read and write the matching slots: date is the time\nslot and label the target."},"681":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#describe","content":"Describe `SCHEMA.TABLE` (or a dataset id's table): the approved descriptor when the table still matches it,\nelse a fresh draft. Uses the connection given, else opens the kit's. Only SELECTs run."},"682":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#Draft","content":"A descriptor proposed for a table (status draft), or the approved one describe() returned."},"683":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#Draft","content":"Member"},"684":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#Draft","content":"What it is"},"685":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#Draft","content":"`id`"},"686":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/describe#Draft","content":"`table`"},"687":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/describe-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/d