taset` reads the\ncurrent one before it falls back to a shipped descriptor."},"726":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store#approved_datasets","content":"Every dataset with an approved column map, newest approval first: \\{id, table, version, approved_at}."},"727":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store#approved_datasets","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"728":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store#column_map_versions","content":"Every saved version of a dataset's column map, oldest first: \\{version, approved_at, roles, slots, evidence} -\nwhat approving one of them again (RoleReview\\.approve) would restore."},"729":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store#current_version","content":"The approved version's number from `current`, or None when there is none (or the file does not hold one)."},"730":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store#descriptor_store_dir","content":"The folder that holds the versions of the descriptor `id` (whether or not it exists yet); an id that is not\na dataset id is refused, so no path is built from it."},"731":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/descriptor-store#list_versions","content":"The version numbers stored for `id` (every v\\<n>.yaml), ascending; empty when none is stored."},"732":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","type":"page","content":"Documentation","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs"},"733":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","content":"The notebooks' documentation, opened from a cell: nb.docs()."},"734":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#Docs","content":"nb.Docs"},"735":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#docs","content":"nb.docs"},"736":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","content":"The documentation is a site of plain files the kit ships (`notebook/docs/site` in the kit copy): pages, styles and\na search index, built ahead of time. This module serves that folder from this Python on this computer only\n(the loopback address, a free port) and shows it in a frame under the cell, so reading and searching need no internet, no Node\nand no second install. The server starts on the first call and stops with the kernel."},"737":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","content":"A command's page is found in the site's own list (`commands.json`, written from `exakit.nb`'s `__all__` when the\nsite is built), so every public helper has one. Anything else is handed to the site's search."},"738":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#Docs","content":"What `nb.docs()` returns: the documentation at `url`. A notebook shows it in a frame under the cell;\n`open()` opens it in a browser tab."},"739":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#Docs","content":"Member"},"740":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#Docs","content":"What it is"},"741":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#Docs","content":"`open() -> Docs`"},"742":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#Docs","content":"Open the page in the default browser."},"743":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#docs","content":"Open the notebooks' documentation: all of it, one command's page, one page, or a search."},"744":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/docs#docs","content":"`what` is nothing (the section of the persona whose notebook this is, else the start page), a helper or its name (`nb.describe`, `\"describe\"`: that command's page),\na page's address (`\"concepts/descriptor\"`), or any other words (searched, typos forgiven). The result shows\nunder the cell in a frame `height` pixels tall; `browser=True` opens a browser tab too. Served from this\ncomputer only, from files the kit ships: nothing is fetched from the internet."},"745":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","type":"page","content":"Hand-off bundle","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle"},"746":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","content":"Hand off: everything a colleague needs to repeat a piece of work, in one folder (and one zip)."},"747":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#handoff_bundle","content":"nb.handoff_bundle"},"748":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"nb.HandoffBundle"},"749":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","content":"The folder holds the approved column map (`descriptor.yaml`), the schema map when there is one\n(`schema-map.json`), every query the workflow ran with its digest and row count (`queries.sql`), the workflow log\nas it is (`workflow.jsonl`) and a `README.md` that says what the data is, which column map version the numbers rest\non, which questions were approved, which dashboards were published and how to repeat it. Nothing in it is a password:\nthe log is already written without one, and the connection is the kit's."},"750":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","content":"This is the Data Scientist's hand-off. The ML Engineer's training handoff (one JSON file with the feature view and the\nsplit, `nb.write_handoff`) is a different thing with its own folder."},"751":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#handoff_bundle","content":"Write the bundle for `ds` and the workflow (the active one, else the last one on this machine, else none) into\n`folder` (default `$EXAKIT_HOME/bundles/<workflow id>/`; a bundle for no workflow is named after the dataset)\nand, with `zip_it`, a zip beside it. The active workflow's log gets a `handoff` line with the path."},"752":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#handoff_bundle","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/03_share`"},"753":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"Where the bundle is and what is in it."},"754":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"Member"},"755":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"What it is"},"756":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`path`"},"757":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`Path`"},"758":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`zip_path`"},"759":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"\\`Path"},"760":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"None\\`"},"761":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`workflow_id`"},"762":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"\\`str"},"763":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"None\\`"},"764":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`files`"},"765":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`list[str]`"},"766":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`summary`"},"767":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-bundle#HandoffBundle","content":"`list[str]`"},"768":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","type":"page","content":"Training handoff","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff"},"769":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","content":"The handoff from the Data Scientist to the ML Engineer (DS-3 -> ML-3, design 4): one JSON file that holds everything 01_train needs to train without opening the descriptor - which descriptor version and digest it came from, a digest of the data, the feature view built from the roles (as CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW SQL), the label and its positive class, the training SELECT with a reproducible time split, and the input and output schemas."},"770":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#handoff_from","content":"nb.handoff_from"},"771":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#handoff_is_stale","content":"nb.handoff_is_stale"},"772":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#read_handoff","content":"nb.read_handoff"},"773":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#write_handoff","content":"nb.write_handoff"},"774":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","content":"The handoff from the Data Scientist to the ML Engineer (DS-3 -> ML-3, design 4): one JSON file that holds everything\n`01_train` needs to train without opening the descriptor - which descriptor version and digest it came from, a digest\nof the data, the feature view built from the roles (as `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` SQL), the label and its positive\nclass, the training SELECT with a reproducible time split, and the input and output schemas. A descriptor without a date\nrole has no time split: the handoff is refused with the fix (`split=\"random\"` for a reproducible hash split, or a\ndate role) - a random split is never silent, and `01_train` refuses one the file does not mark as asked for."},"775":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","content":"The feature view is SQL only - category one-hot over the top-20 values plus OTHER, date -> year / month / ISO day of\nweek / days since the first date, text -> LENGTH, entity -> frequency - so a model that is linear over these columns can\nbe scored by Rust on the very same view (ML-5): TF-IDF stays out of it (the client-side model in explore keeps it);\ntop-k token flags computed in SQL are the deferred next step and are recorded as such in the file. The view is not\ncreated here: the ML quickstart and 01_train create it, with the admin profile."},"776":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","content":"The file names a table, columns, SQL and digests, never a host, a user or a password; the kit's secret-grep test\ncovers the folder. A workflow that is active gets one `handoff` line in its log (X-1)."},"777":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#handoff_from","content":"The handoff record for `ds` as design 4 shapes it, built now and returned, nothing written: the descriptor's\nid, version, digest (`digest_kind` says whether it is the table digest or the file's) and source; the data\ndigest (`data_digest_kind`); the feature view; the label and its positive class (`label` overrides it);\nthe split (`time` over the date role by default; `split=\"random\"` for a hash split, the only way to get one -\nwithout a date role and without that, a ValueError names the fix; `split.explicit` records the choice) and\n`train_share`; the training SQL; input and output schemas. `workflow_id` defaults to the active workflow's."},"778":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#handoff_is_stale","content":"None when `handoff` still describes `ds` and its data; else the line 01_train prints before it refuses:\nthe descriptor's version or digest changed (recomputed from `ds`: the same kind the handoff recorded), or - with\na connection - the data digest no longer matches. The fix is in the line."},"779":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#handoff_is_stale","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"780":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#read_handoff","content":"The handoff as a dict: from a path to the file, from `<id>-v<n>` (that version's file), or from a descriptor\nid (the file with the highest version in the handoffs folder). None there is a FileNotFoundError saying how to\nmake one."},"781":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#read_handoff","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"782":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/handoff#write_handoff","content":"Build the handoff (handoff_from) and write it to `$EXAKIT_HOME/handoffs/<id>-v<n>.json` - the folder 0700,\nthe file 0600, replaced whole (a temporary file renamed over it) so a reader never sees half of one. The active\nworkflow's log gets a `handoff` line with the path and the descriptor's id and version. Returns the path."},"783":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","type":"page","content":"All commands","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference"},"784":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Every public helper of exakit.nb, 111 in all, with the page that documents it."},"785":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Every notebook starts with `import exakit.nb as nb`. Each name below is one call a cell can make, and the same\ncall a guided card makes behind its buttons."},"786":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Command"},"787":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What it does"},"788":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.addon_ready`"},"789":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Make an add-on usable from here: install it when it is not (`exakit marketplace <addon>`), start it when it is a service and stopped (`exakit start <addon>`), and say its state and address."},"790":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.addons`"},"791":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The marketplace's add-ons as `exakit marketplace --list --json` reports them: \\{id, name, about, status, installed, version, url}, and `offered`: False for one the kit's catalog does not offer yet (its marketplace/catalog.json says \"visible\": false, so no marketplace screen lists it)."},"792":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.ai_clients`"},"793":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The AI clients the kit can connect to the database (its MCP adapters), each \\{id, name, connected}, with connected from `exakit mcp-status --json`."},"794":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.approved_datasets`"},"795":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Every dataset with an approved column map, newest approval first: \\{id, table, version, approved_at}."},"796":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.ask`"},"797":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Draft SQL from roles and the user's opted-in model endpoint; `proposed_sql` supports manual drafting."},"798":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.check_bucket`"},"799":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The deployment's bucket directory exists on this machine where the kit says it is, and - given a connection - a UDF sees it at its /buckets path too (skipped, with a note, when the container check fails)."},"800":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.check_connection`"},"801":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The database answers: its time, this session's id and its version, as one row (and one line)."},"802":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.check_container`"},"803":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The container behind `alias` runs a smoke UDF, and it has every package training needs."},"804":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.check_mlflow`"},"805":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Check the destination runs will really use: configured server, kit server, or local store."},"806":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.check_model_compatibility`"},"807":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Refuse a pickle whose scikit-learn version differs before any scoring SQL runs."},"808":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.chosen_dataset`"},"809":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The dataset a notebook works on: `name` when it is set; with None, the one approved last in a quickstart (so picking fraud_transactions there carries on here), else amazon_sales."},"810":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.clean_path`"},"811":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A path pasted into a cell, made usable: quotes and spaces around it, a `file://` link, the shell's backslash escapes (`My\\ Data`, from a drag into a terminal) and `~` are undone."},"812":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.column_map_versions`"},"813":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Every saved version of a dataset's column map, oldest first: \\{version, approved_at, roles, slots, evidence} - what approving one of them again (RoleReview\\.approve) would restore."},"814":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.components`"},"815":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The kit's parts as `exakit version --json` reports them: \\{id, installed, available, status, add_on, ownership, remedy}, with a status of current, ahead, update_available, available (an add-on not installed) or missing; `available` is the version the kit would install or update to."},"816":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.confirm_send`"},"817":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Before sampled rows go to a model endpoint: True at once for a table in the database; for a live source (the descriptor names a source) it names the source and asks, and only a yes sends."},"818":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.connect`"},"819":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A pyexasol connection to the local database, opened from the kit's encrypted store, pinned to the database's TLS certificate once the kit has recorded it."},"820":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.connect_source`"},"821":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Connect an external source as a virtual schema, from a notebook cell."},"822":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.connected_sources`"},"823":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The virtual schemas in the database (external sources) with their number of tables; empty when there is none."},"824":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.connector_inputs`"},"825":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What `exakit connect <connector>` asks, from the kit's source engine (`inputs`: what its connect form reads, in the form's order)."},"826":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.connectors`"},"827":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The kinds of external source `exakit connect` takes, as its own menu lists them (the kit's source engine, `catalog`): \\{id, name, summary, aliases, tier, status, version, gate} - `version` the adapter the kit pins, `gate` why one is not available yet (empty when it is)."},"828":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.continue_workflow`"},"829":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-45","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The workflow already going, without an id to paste: this kernel's, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else the last one started or resumed on this machine (a quickstart starts one); a new one named `name` only when there is none."},"830":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-46","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.count_name`"},"831":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-47","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The count column, named after what is counted: ORDER_LINES, STORE_WEEKS; ROW_COUNT when the descriptor does not say (ROWS is an SQL word)."},"832":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-48","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.current_version`"},"833":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-49","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The approved version's number from `current`, or None when there is none (or the file does not hold one)."},"834":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-50","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.current_workflow`"},"835":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-51","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The active workflow id: the session's, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else None."},"836":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-52","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.dash_tools`"},"837":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-53","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The notebook's Dash Server tool adapter; each call is an MCP tool call."},"838":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-54","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.DashTools`"},"839":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-55","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Synchronous adapter for notebook cells, which already run an event loop."},"840":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-56","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.data_checks`"},"841":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-57","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Prepare: one row per finding - CHECK, COLUMN_NAME, ROWS_AFFECTED, PCT, MEANS - for repeated keys, repeated identifiers, exact copies of a row, empty cells, placeholder values and a rare label."},"842":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-58","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.data_map`"},"843":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-59","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The semantic map of the database: every table by origin (sample, local, source) with its rows, columns, column-map state and roles, then the links between tables - declared, found by an approved schema map, or a shared key-like column name across two tables (marked possible)."},"844":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-60","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.DataMap`"},"845":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-61","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What data_map found: tables, columns and links, each a list of dicts; DataFrames through the properties."},"846":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-62","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.Dataset`"},"847":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-63","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A validated descriptor whose every role the database holds, with the SQL names the notebooks build queries from."},"848":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-64","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.dataset`"},"849":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-65","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The dataset `name`, checked against the database: a kit dataset id, a descriptor file or its folder, or a data file of your own (CSV, Parquet or JSON) with its descriptor beside it, which is loaded first (load_own_file)."},"850":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-66","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.describe`"},"851":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-67","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Describe `SCHEMA.TABLE` (or a dataset id's table): the approved descriptor when the table still matches it, else a fresh draft."},"852":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-68","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.describe_schema`"},"853":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-69","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The schema of `dataset_or_schema` (a dataset, or a schema name) as found now: its tables, rows and keys, and every many-to-one link between them with its evidence."},"854":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-70","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.descriptor_store_dir`"},"855":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-71","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The folder that holds the versions of the descriptor `id` (whether or not it exists yet); an id that is not a dataset id is refused, so no path is built from it."},"856":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-72","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.DescriptorNotApproved`"},"857":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-73","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A step that needs an approved descriptor was given a draft; the message says how to approve it."},"858":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-74","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.Docs`"},"859":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-75","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What `nb.docs()` returns: the documentation at `url`."},"860":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-76","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.docs`"},"861":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-77","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Open the notebooks' documentation: all of it, one command's page, one page, or a search."},"862":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-78","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.Draft`"},"863":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-79","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A descriptor proposed for a table (status draft), or the approved one describe() returned."},"864":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-80","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.draft_question`"},"865":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-81","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A Proposal for `question` drafted by rules from the column map (no AI model): read-only SQL, with the drafter's assumptions, not approved yet."},"866":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-82","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.exakit`"},"867":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-83","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Run `exakit <args>` and show its output line by line as it comes (`show=False` keeps it quiet); the KitRun says how it ended."},"868":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-84","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.example_questions`"},"869":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-85","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Up to three questions this dataset's approved roles can answer, in its own column names."},"870":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-86","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.feature_ideas`"},"871":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-87","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Feature ideas for this lab's data, each with the SQL that would make it: try one with try_feature."},"872":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-88","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.first`"},"873":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-89","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The first dataset that was loaded, in the order given; says which one is used."},"874":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-90","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.forget_model`"},"875":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-91","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Delete what use_model(..., remember=True) saved (the model, Langfuse, or both) and clear it from this kernel."},"8