entist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","content":"They are the environment variables `exakit notebook` already reads (EXAKIT_MODEL_ID, EXAKIT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL,\nEXAKIT_PROVIDER_API_KEY, LANGFUSE\\_\\*, MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI), so a cell is one more way to give them, not another kind of\nsetting. The plain values come from the cell. The keys are asked for in a hidden prompt and kept in this kernel's\nenvironment only: never in the notebook or its outputs, and gone when the kernel stops - unless `remember=True`,\nwhich saves them beside the kit's credentials (readable by this user only, 0600) so every notebook's kernel has them\n(`import exakit.nb` loads them; `forget_model()` deletes them). A key already set (by\nthe shell that started JupyterLab, or an earlier run of the cell) is not asked again - unless the address it was for\nchanged. Empty values change nothing, so a cell left as shipped is a no-op and a headless run never waits on a prompt."},"1336":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#forget_model","content":"Delete what use_model(..., remember=True) saved (the model, Langfuse, or both) and clear it from this kernel."},"1337":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#forget_model","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1338":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#model_setup","content":"Set up your model and Langfuse for this kernel, and say how to set them for every notebook. Inside a notebook\n(JupyterLab or Marimo) it first asks for what is missing - the model id and address, the Langfuse address, then\neach key in a hidden box; Enter skips one. `ask=False` only reports; a script or test never waits on a prompt.\nThen it prints what is set and, for anything still missing, the terminal lines for this machine (Windows, Mac,\nLinux or WSL). Prints values, never a key; returns \\{\"machine\", \"set\", \"missing\", \"lines\", \"asked\"}."},"1339":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#model_setup","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"1340":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#use_mlflow","content":"The MLflow server this kernel records runs to: `tracking_uri` (empty: the kit's own MLflow, or what the shell\nset); `login=True` asks for the server's username and password (hidden). Prints where runs go, never a password."},"1341":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#use_mlflow","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`, `ml-engineer/01_train`"},"1342":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#use_model","content":"Your model and Langfuse tracing for this kernel. `model_id` and `provider_base_url` (a Chat Completions base\nURL) set the model and ask for its API key (Enter for none: a local server); `langfuse_base_url` turns tracing on\nand asks for its two keys. Prints what is in use, never a key; returns that summary."},"1343":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/setup-env#use_model","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"1344":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","type":"page","content":"Share a dashboard","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/share"},"1345":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share","content":"Prepare a governed Dash Server dashboard and promote only a reviewed preview."},"1346":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#share","content":"nb.share"},"1347":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"nb.ShareDraft"},"1348":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share","content":"`tool` is a callable for the registered dash-server MCP tools. Notebook cells\nuse the kit-managed MCP endpoint through `dash_tools()`.\nThe dashboard itself queries Exasol through Dash Server's server-side profile."},"1349":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#share","content":"Make a draft from approved data and inspected SQL; measure=count enables count totals and composition."},"1350":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#share","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/03_share`"},"1351":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft