rofile_name: str='starter-kit', windows: bool \\| None=None) -> str`"},"1381":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"Create and health-check a preview; on Windows use build + healthcheck."},"1382":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"`confirm(tool: Tool, figures_checked: bool=False) -> str`"},"1383":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"Promote the exact healthy preview after a human checks its figures."},"1384":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"page","content":"External sources","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources"},"1385":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","content":"External sources from a notebook cell: connect one, and read what a cell was given."},"1386":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#clean_path","content":"nb.clean_path"},"1387":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#connect_source","content":"nb.connect_source"},"1388":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#read_connection_string","content":"nb.read_connection_string"},"1389":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#source_engine","content":"nb.source_engine"},"1390":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceProblem","content":"nb.SourceProblem"},"1391":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"nb.SourceTest"},"1392":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#test_source","content":"nb.test_source"},"1393":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","content":"connect_source runs `exakit connect <connector> --name <name> ... --password-stdin --yes --json`. The password is\nasked in a hidden box and goes to the command on standard input: never into the cell, the command line or a log."},"1394":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#clean_path","content":"A path pasted into a cell, made usable: quotes and spaces around it, a `file://` link, the shell's\nbackslash escapes (`My\\ Data`, from a drag into a terminal) and `~` are undone. Empty stays empty."},"1395":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#connect_source","content":"Connect an external source as a virtual schema, from a notebook cell. `connector` is the kit's id or alias\n(`postgresql`, `pg`, `mysql`, `snowflake` ...; `exakit help connect` lists them), `name` becomes the\nschema `VS_<NAME>`. Give the source's connection string as `url` (a JDBC URL, `postgres://...`), or each\ninput as a keyword (`host=`, `database=`, `schema=`, `user=` ...; the connector's skill lists them).\nThe password is asked in a hidden box (Enter: none), or read from `password_file`; a password inside `url` is\ntaken out of it and used, never shown. Marimo has no hidden prompt: pass a password field as `password`\n(`mo.ui.text(kind=\"password\")`, its value is read) or a `password_file`. `dry_run` checks the inputs and\nconnects nothing. A connector with several kinds of source in one takes its settings as keywords too\n(`catalog=\"unity\", files=\"s3\"` for a Lakehouse; nb.connector_inputs lists them). A source with a second secret\n(a Lakehouse catalog login plus storage keys) takes it as `storage_secret_file`, or as `storage_secret` (the\ntext, a Marimo password field, or a function that asks for it): it reaches the kit in a file only this user can\nread, removed as soon as the kit has read it. Returns the schema name (`VS_SALES`) when connected, None for a dry run; raises SourceProblem with the kit's reason otherwise."},"1396":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#read_connection_string","content":"Read a source's connection string exactly as `exakit connect --url` does: it is handed to the kit's engine\n(its `paste` command, on standard input, never as an argument). Returns \\{connector, values, notes, dropped,\nmasked, credential_in_string, secret_input, missing}: `values` by input name, each checked as if typed;\n`masked` the string with every credential as \\*\\*\\*\\*; `missing` the connector's required inputs the string does\nnot give (and no default covers). The string's password is used by nb.connect_source(url=...) and is never\nreturned, printed or logged here. For a connector with settings (a Lakehouse's `catalog=`, `files=`) give the\nones already chosen: a setting the string itself shows (an s3:// path\nis a folder with no catalog) comes back in `values`, and `missing` is what that combination still needs."},"1397":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#source_engine","content":"Ask the kit's own source engine (setup/virtual-schemas/engine/cli.py, the coordinator behind `exakit connect`\nand `exakit source`) one of the questions its connect form asks, and return its --json answer:"},"1398":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#source_engine","content":"Run as the kit's shell runs it: the kit's Python where it is installed, isolated (-I), with this installation's\ndefinitions and home. None of these four touches the database. A refusal is a SourceProblem in the engine's\nwords, with its remedy."},"1399":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceProblem","content":"A source cell that cannot go on, said in one short message: no traceback in a notebook."},"1400":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"What test_source found, one check per line: (what was checked, passed, what it said)."},"1401":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"Member"},"1402":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"What it is"},"1403":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`connector`"},"1404":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`str`"},"1405":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`name`"},"1406":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`str`"},"1407":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`checks`"},"1408":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`list[tuple[str, bool, str]]`"},"1409":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`ok`"},"1410":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#test_source","content":"Test a source before connecting it, changing nothing: first the kit's own check of every input\n(`exakit connect ... --dry-run`), then whether this computer reaches the source's host and port. No password is\nneeded or sent. The sign-in itself is checked by nb.connect_source, from the database (exakit source check)."},"1411":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","type":"page","content":"Themes in text (AI)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes"},"1412":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","content":"What the texts on each side of the label are about, read by your model and traced to your Langfuse."},"1413":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes#themes","content":"nb.themes"},"1414":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","content":"One model call per side (label = 1, label = 0): the model sorts that side's texts into two to four themes\nand answers in JSON, so the result is a table - theme, how many texts, their share, an example - with a note in plain\nwords under it. A theme found on one side only is the clue: what those texts are about that the others are not."},"1415":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","content":"With Langfuse set up (nb.trace), both calls are one trace, `explore-themes`, each call named after its side, with\nwhat was sent, the answer, tokens, cost and time, and two scores to compare models and runs by: `valid_json` (1 when\nevery answer could be read) and `texts_placed` (the share of texts the model gave a theme)."},"1416":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes#themes","content":"Sort each side's texts into themes with `endpoint` = (client, model) from nb.model_client(); return the table\n(a pandas DataFrame when pandas is there, else a list of rows) and print the note. None without an endpoint."},"1417":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes#themes","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1418":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"page","content":"Workflows","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow"},"1419":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"One workflow id on everything (X-1): workflow() starts or resumes one, and every helper that does something appends a line to its log while it is active - a statement, a trace, an MLflow run, a descriptor draft or approval, a handoff, a dashboard revision, a model put."},"1420":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#continue_workflow","content":"nb.continue_workflow"},"1421":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#current_workflow","content":"nb.current_workflow"},"1422":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#last_workflow","content":"nb.last_workflow"},"1423":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#list_workflows","content":"nb.list_workflows"},"1424":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_event","content":"nb.log_event"},"1425":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_sql","content":"nb.log_sql"},"1426":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow","content":"nb.workflow"},"1427":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow_log","content":"nb.workflow_log"},"1428":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"One workflow id on everything (X-1): `workflow()` starts or resumes one, and every helper that does something\nappends a line to its log while it is active - a statement, a trace, an MLflow run, a descriptor draft or approval, a\nhandoff, a dashboard revision, a model put. Without a workflow nothing is written: there are no implicit workflows."},"1429":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"A notebook never needs an id pasted in: the quickstart starts the work and every later notebook continues it with\n`continue_workflow`, which takes this kernel's workflow, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else the\nlast one started or resumed on this machine ($EXAKIT_HOME/last-workflow), and starts a new one only when there is none."},"1430":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"The id is `wf-YYYYMMDD-<6 hex>`, kept in the session store and in EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID so a child process (a CLI call\nfrom a notebook) inherits it. The log is `$EXAKIT_HOME/workflows/<id>.jsonl` (EXAKIT_HOME default\n\\~/.exasol-starter-kit), append-only, one JSON object per line: `{ts, workflow_id, kind, ...payload}`; the folder is\n0700 and the file 0600, each line one O_APPEND write so two kernels on one workflow never interleave. A log that\ncannot be written warns and the cell goes on: logging never fails the work it describes."},"1431":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"Credential-shaped payload keys are checked recursively, including JSON-encoded metadata strings. A secret-named key\nor a DSN containing a password is refused (a\nValueError - the caller's mistake, before anything is written). SQL text is screened rather than refused: a statement\nthat mentions PASSWORD, API_KEY, IDENTIFIED BY and the like - or carries a DSN with a password - is logged with its\ntext replaced by `<redacted: credential-like SQL>` and `redacted: true`, its digest kept, and one warning; the\nlogger never fails the query it records, which has already run. Other SQL text is kept so the user can find the\nquery again."},"1432":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"`python -m exakit_nb.workflow list|show <id> [--json]` is what `exakit workflow` runs."},"1433":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#continue_workflow","content":"The workflow already going, without an id to paste: this kernel's, else the one inherited through\nEXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else the last one started or resumed on this machine (a quickstart starts one); a new one named\n`name` only when there is none. Says which, and returns the id."},"1434":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#continue_workflow","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/01_train`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"1435":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#current_workflow","content":"The active workflow id: the session's, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else None."},"1436":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#current_workflow","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"1437":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#last_workflow","content":"The workflow started or resumed last on this machine, when its log is still there; else None."},"1438":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#list_workflows","content":"One summary per log in the workflows folder, oldest first: id, name (from its start line), started, last\n(first and last timestamps) and events (the line count). An unreadable log is skipped."},"1439":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#list_workflows","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1440":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_event","content":"Append one line to the active workflow's log; nothing when no workflow is active. A credential-named payload\nkey or a DSN with a password is a ValueError (the caller's mistake); credential-like statement text is logged\nredacted with a warning (never an exception: the statement already ran); a log that cannot be written is a warning\n(the environment's)."},"1441":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_event","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"1442":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_sql","content":"Log a statement sql() ran: the session and statement ids that find it in the database's audit log, the\nstatement's SHA-256 (what traces and runs carry), how many rows came back, and the statement text - redacted, with\na warning, when it looks credential-bearing (a PASSWORD or API_KEY column, say); this never raises, the query has\nalready run. No-op without a workflow; the statement id is looked up on the connection unless given."},"1443":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_sql","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/01_train`"},"1444":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow","content":"Start a workflow (a new id, a `start` line in its log) or, with `resume`, continue an existing one. The id\nbecomes the session's and EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID's, and is returned. Resuming an id whose log does not exist is a\nValueError naming the path, so a typo never starts an empty log under a made-up id."},"1445":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"1446":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow_log","content":"Every line of a workflow's log, in order. A missing log is a FileNotFoundError naming the path."},"1447":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow_log","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1448":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"page","content":"Guided and Code","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Start here"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code"},"1449":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","content":"The cards each notebook opens with, the Code switch, and how a button and a cell are the same call."},"1450":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"The guided view"},"1451":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"The Code switch"},"1452":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-call-two-ways","content":"One call, two ways"},"1453":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"The Home card"},"1454":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-workflow-per-start","content":"One workflow per start"},"1455":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"Each Data Scientist notebook opens with cards that do the page's steps with buttons and forms."},"1456":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"Notebook"},"1457":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"Its cards open with"},"1458":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`00_quickstart`"},"1459":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.start()`"},"1460":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`01_explore`"},"1461":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.explore()`"},"1462":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`02_ask_your_data`"},"1463":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.ask()`"},"1464":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`03_share`"},"1465":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.share()`"},"1466":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"Every card has a **Guided / Code** switch at its top right."},"1467":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"**Code** turns that card, in place, into its code: what it ran this session, in order, and the exact call behind each control. Each block has **Copy as cell**."},"1468":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"**Guided** turns it back. Only that card changes. The connection, the chosen data and the approvals stay as they are."},"1469":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"The notebook's own cells sit under **The code behind this page**. In the kit's JupyterLab they are hidden until you choose **Show all the notebook's code cells** at the foot of a card's Code view. In Marimo the cells open with their code visible."},"1470":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-call-two-ways","content":"Every button, form and choice on a card is one `exakit.nb` call, and the same call is a cell in the notebook's code section. Clicking **Approve** and running `role_review.approve(...)` do the same thing."},"1471":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-call-two-ways","content":"What a card shows is read from the kit when it draws: the datasets, connectors, add-ons and notebooks are not written into the card. A connector added to the kit appears in the form the same day."},"1472":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"The first card of the quickstart is the kit itself. It has two tabs."},"1473":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"**Your kit:** what is installed and running, the loaded datasets, your approved column maps and your workflows."},"1474":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"**Marketplace:** every add-on with **Install**, **Start** and **Update** buttons. They run `nb.addon_ready(id)` and `nb.kit_update(id)`, which is what 