k. The quickstart starts it and the other notebooks continue it. You never paste an id."],[52,"A certificate cannot be verified"],[211,"A column whose values almost decide the target on their own would make a model look better than it is. These columns are listed and left out of the model."],[349,"A command run from a cell has no terminal, so a question it would ask takes its default. Give a choice up front instead: `nb.exakit(\"mcp-setup\", env={\"EXAKIT_MCP_CLIENTS\": \"claude\"})`."],[737,"A command's page is found in the site's own list (`commands.json`, written from `exakit.nb`'s `__all__` when the\nsite is built), so every public helper has one. Anything else is handed to the site's search."],[1499,"A connection, a loaded dataset and an approved column map"],[1061,"A connector with several kinds of source in one (Lakehouse: Iceberg REST, Unity, Glue or a plain folder, on S3 or\nAzure) has settings that decide what it asks. `tree` is those settings as the connect menu's tree (a catalog,\nand under it the files it can read), each node with the settings its pick gives; give them here\n(`connector_inputs(\"lakehouse\", catalog=\"unity\", files=\"s3\")`) and `inputs` are that combination's.\n`settings` are the ones in force (given, or the kit's default) and `setting_inputs` the setting questions\nthemselves, each with its `choices`, their `choice_labels` and the default in force. Every other connector\nhas an empty `tree` and no `setting_inputs`."],[253,"A CSV, Parquet, JSON or Excel file, a folder of them, or a table already in the database. Files are loaded with the kit's own loader, the one `exakit data-load` runs."],[969,"A dashboard prepared from an approved dataset and one query."],[1351,"A dashboard prepared from an approved dataset and one query. `preview()` puts it on Dash Server as a preview;\n`confirm(..., figures_checked=True)` publishes it, and only after a person checked the preview's figures."],[214,"A dashboard that goes up as a preview first, and one folder that lets a colleague repeat the work."],[215,"A dashboard, preview first"],[254,"A database or lake elsewhere: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Snowflake and others. The kit connects it as a **virtual schema**: its tables appear in your local Exasol as `VS_<NAME>` and are read from the source when you query them. Nothing is copied."],[330,"A dataset that is not loaded yet is loaded first. Nothing else is needed."],[1211,"A dataset the kit offers (`amazon_sales`, `fraud_transactions`): used as it is when it is loaded, else loaded\nfirst with `exakit data-load <id>` (the cell waits for it), then checked against the database. None skips it."],[911,"A dataset the kit offers (`amazon_sales`, `fraud_transactions`): used as it is when it is loaded, else loaded first with `exakit data-load <id>` (the cell waits for it), then checked against the database."],[604,"A dataset the notebooks run on: its descriptor read, validated by the kit's own rules, held against the database, and the roles turned into SQL names, so one notebook runs unchanged on any dataset whose descriptor is valid."],[325,"A dataset with no target skips the model steps and says so. Choose a target in the column map to run them."],[132,"A date or timestamp"],[682,"A descriptor proposed for a table (status draft), or the approved one describe() returned."],[863,"A descriptor proposed for a table (status draft), or the approved one describe() returned."],[183,"A descriptor starts as a **draft**: the kit's proposal. A proposal can be wrong. In `amazon_sales`, `STATUS` gives the answer away; the kit warns about it and the model leaves it out."],[136,"A few repeated values"],[1164,"A file loaded as text (every column VARCHAR, as CSVs often are), blank cells, placeholder values and rows copied twice\nall make a result quietly wrong. typed_view() reads the table - not just its names - and proposes one view over it:"],[331,"A file or a folder:"],[917,"A file that has been loaded but has not yet received an approved descriptor."],[1149,"A file that has been loaded but has not yet received an approved descriptor."],[91,"A key is never written into a cell, the code view or the workflow log."],[102,"A kit dataset"],[243,"A kit dataset"],[487,"A kit notebook you did not edit is refreshed when the kit's version changes."],[281,"A log that cannot be written warns and the cell goes on. Logging never fails the work it describes."],[357,"A model is optional. It is used to draft SQL in Ask and to sort texts into themes in Explore. Any endpoint that speaks the Chat Completions API works: an external provider or a model on your own machine."],[38,"A model step is skipped"],[438,"A notebook is cells that call the helpers. A card is a form that calls the same helpers. Neither talks to the database on its own."],[1429,"A notebook never needs an id pasted in: the quickstart starts the work and every later notebook continues it with\n`continue_workflow`, which takes this kernel's workflow, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else the\nlast one started or resumed on this machine ($EXAKIT_HOME/last-workflow), and starts a new one only when there is none."],[489,"A notebook you deleted is not copied back."],[488,"A notebook you edited, or a file of your own, is never overwritten."],[134,"A number to add up or average"],[265,"A password inside a connection string is used and never shown."],[263,"A password is asked in a hidden box and handed to `exakit connect` on standard input."],[1394,"A path pasted into a cell, made usable: quotes and spaces around it, a `file://` link, the shell's\nbackslash escapes (`My\\ Data`, from a drag into a terminal) and `~` are undone. Empty stays empty."],[811,"A path pasted into a cell, made usable: quotes and spaces around it, a `file://` link, the shell's backslash escapes (`My\\ Data`, from a drag into a terminal) and `~` are undone."],[223,"A preview that was not checked is never promoted. In automated runs the check is never set, so nothing is published without a person."],[1192,"A Proposal for `question` drafted by rules from the column map (no AI model): read-only SQL, with the\ndrafter's assumptions, not approved yet. Approve and run it as any proposal."],[865,"A Proposal for `question` drafted by rules from the column map (no AI model): read-only SQL, with the drafter's assumptions, not approved yet."],[309,"A proposed query can be wrong: a wrong column, a missing filter. Read it."],[1508,"A published dashboard and one folder a colleague can repeat the work from"],[546,"A pyexasol connection to the local database, opened from the kit's encrypted store, pinned to the database's\nTLS certificate once the kit has recorded it. Exasol's usage telemetry stays off unless EXASOL_TELEMETRY_DISABLE\nwas already set."],[819,"A pyexasol connection to the local database, opened from the kit's encrypted store, pinned to the database's TLS certificate once the kit has recorded it."],[951,"A question with the SQL proposed for it."],[498,"A question with the SQL proposed for it. Nothing runs until `approve()` accepts that exact text; `edit()` replaces\nthe SQL and removes the approval; `run()` runs the approved text through the kit's read-only service."],[1226,"A result column named after a data column: `CANCELLED` + `PCT` -> `CANCELLED_PCT`; quotes, dots and\nspaces become underscores, so the name works unquoted in SQL."],[933,"A result column named after a data column: `CANCELLED` + `PCT` -> `CANCELLED_PCT`; quotes, dots and spaces become underscores, so the name works unquoted in SQL."],[114,"A role no column fits is never guessed. `dataset.has(...)` is false, the step that needs it skips, and it says why."],[79,"A sample of texts, on each side of the target"],[266,"A second secret (a Lakehouse's storage keys) goes to the kit in a private file, never on a command line."],[280,"A secret-named value or a connection string with a password is refused before anything is written. SQL that mentions a password or an API key is 