nal), `VS_<NAME>` alone (its one table, or a list of them), or a descriptor file whose\nfact_table is in a source. None skips it and lists the sources there are. A name that cannot be used stops the\ncell with one line naming what is there and how to connect one; the table is read once (one row) to prove it."],[94,"A table plus its approved column map, which is what every notebook step reads."],[333,"A table that is already in the database:"],[1278,"A table's column map says what its columns are; the schema map says how the schema's tables fit together - every\ntable with its rows and key, and every many-to-one link between them, declared by the database or found (a column\nthat names another table's key and whose every value is in it), each with its evidence. The kit's describe service\ndoes the work (setup/lib/descriptor/schema.py); this module shows it in a notebook and turns it into a dataset:"],[39,"A text step is skipped"],[201,"A typed, cleaned view"],[613,"A validated descriptor whose every role the database holds, with the SQL names the notebooks build queries from."],[847,"A validated descriptor whose every role the database holds, with the SQL names the notebooks build queries from."],[396,"A whole new module gets its own reference page automatically, titled from its file name. Give it a proper title and a place in the order by adding one line to `PAGES` in `tools/nb_docs.py`."],[1481,"Access"],[384,"Add a command"],[391,"Add a function to a module in `notebook/package/exakit_nb/`, with a docstring. The first sentence becomes its one-line summary here; the rest becomes its reference text. Indented lines in a docstring are shown as code."],[1322,"Add a link the search missed: `link(\"ORDERS.CUSTOMER_REF\", \"CUSTOMERS.ID\")`."],[385,"Add an exakit.nb helper, wire it to a card, and get its documentation for free."],[394,"Add one entry to `actions.ACTIONS` in `exakit_guide/actions.py`: the code and the notebook it belongs to. Have the screen call `actions.run(...)`."],[393,"Add the call to the code section of the notebook it belongs to, guarded by a variable when it is optional:"],[32,"After an update, nothing changed"],[290,"After approving"],[62,"AI and tracing"],[70,"AI is opt-in. Every notebook runs without a model, and the AI steps are off until you turn them on."],[783,"All commands"],[329,"All of this happens in step 1 of `00_quickstart`. On the **Choose your data** card you pick one of three boxes. The code below is what each box runs."],[49,"Allow this computer's address at the source: a firewall rule, a security group or the server's own access list"],[168,"Amazon sales"],[445,"An action's call exists in its notebook's code section, and calls something `exakit.nb` exports."],[37,"An add-on is missing or stopped"],[1505,"An answer from SQL you read and approved"],[108,"An external source"],[245,"An external source"],[45,"An external source could not be connected. The lines after it give the reason and a fix. The usual causes:"],[151,"Anything over time"],[919,"Append one line to the active workflow's log; nothing when no workflow is active."],[1440,"Append one line to the active workflow's log; nothing when no workflow is active. A credential-named payload\nkey or a DSN with a password is a ValueError (the caller's mistake); credential-like statement text is logged\nredacted with a warning (never an exception: the statement already ran); a log that cannot be written is a warning\n(the environment's)."],[1262,"Apply the reviewed roles (\\{COLUMN: role}, one of the eight; the proposal when None) and slots (\\{slot: COLUMN or None}), then save and comment the approved descriptor."],[298,"Approval checks the data again. A warning about a column that gives the target away is not an error: the column stays in the map and is left out of the model."],[288,"Approve"],[305,"Approve and run"],[14,"Approve it in the quickstart. With `DATASET = None`, the other notebooks follow the dataset approved last when you run their 