t.\nThen it prints what is set and, for anything still missing, the terminal lines for this machine (Windows, Mac,\nLinux or WSL). Prints values, never a key; returns \\{\"machine\", \"set\", \"missing\", \"lines\", \"asked\"}."],[360,"Setting"],[474,"Settings such as the model's id and address"],[1274,"Several tables: the schema around a dataset, and one wide view along its links."],[1488,"Share"],[1344,"Share a dashboard"],[372,"Share a dashboard and hand off"],[240,"Share a dashboard, Dash Server tools, Hand-off bundle, Training handoff."],[213,"Sharing and hand-off"],[7,"Short answers to the questions that come up most."],[146,"Slot"],[119,"Slots: which column each step uses"],[261,"Some combinations have **two secrets**: the catalog login and the storage keys. The login is asked like any password. The storage secret travels in a file only you can read, removed as soon as the kit has read it."],[1416,"Sort each side's texts into themes with `endpoint` = (client, model) from nb.model_client(); return the table\n(a pandas DataFrame when pandas is there, else a list of rows) and print the note. None without an endpoint."],[985,"Sort each side's texts into themes with `endpoint` = (client, model) from nb.model_client(); return the table (a pandas DataFrame when pandas is there, else a list of rows) and print the note."],[78,"Sorts texts into themes"],[100,"Source"],[241,"Sources"],[449,"Sources are `notebook/notebooks/<persona>/<NN>_<name>.py` in jupytext percent format. The `.ipynb` and the Marimo version are built from them:"],[1005,"Start a workflow (a new id, a `start` line in its log) or, with `resume`, continue an existing one."],[1444,"Start a workflow (a new id, a `start` line in its log) or, with `resume`, continue an existing one. The id\nbecomes the session's and EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID's, and is returned. Resuming an id whose log does not exist is a\nValueError naming the path, so a typo never starts an empty log under a made-up id."],[375,"Start Dash Server"