answers: its time, this session's id and its version, as one row (and one line)."],[1207,"The database answers: its time, this session's id and its version, as one row (and one line)."],[36,"The database does not answer"],[431,"The database, connections, loading, connectors, add-ons, the describe service"],[671,"The dataset `name`, checked against the database: a kit dataset id, a descriptor file or its folder, or a data\nfile of your own (CSV, Parquet or JSON) with its descriptor beside it, which is loaded first (load_own_file)."],[849,"The dataset `name`, checked against the database: a kit dataset id, a descriptor file or its folder, or a data file of your own (CSV, Parquet or JSON) with its descriptor beside it, which is loaded first (load_own_file)."],[611,"The dataset a notebook works on: `name` when it is set; with None, the one approved last in a quickstart (so\npicking fraud_transactions there carries on here), else amazon_sales. Says which, and why, in one line."],[809,"The dataset a notebook works on: `name` when it is set; with None, the one approved last in a quickstart (so picking fraud_transactions there carries on here), else amazon_sales."],[464,"The dataset approved last, which the notebooks follow"],[59,"The dataset has no text column. `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions` have none, so the text model and the themes step skip on them and say so."],[523,"The deployment's bucket directory exists on this machine where the kit says it is, and - given a connection -\na UDF sees it at its /buckets path too (skipped, with a note, when the container check fails)."],[799,"The deployment's bucket directory exists on this machine where the kit says it is, and - given a connection - a UDF sees it at its /buckets path too (skipped, with a note, when the container check fails)."],[708,"The descriptor document (a copy)."],[1147,"The descriptor is that mapping of role to column, a descriptor mapping (`schema_version`, `id`, `fact_table`,\n`roles`), or a descriptor file - YAML or JSON; `data/datasets/<id>/descriptor.yaml` in the kit shows the shape -\nwhose fact_table then names the table (`table` may be None). Given as a mapping of roles, they become a\nschema_version 2 \\*\\*draft\\*\\* (version 1, drafted by the user, owned by EXAKIT_DESCRIPTOR_OWNER or the OS user, its\n`source` the file) and are written beside the file as `<name>.descriptor.yaml` (when no descriptor is there yet),\nso `DATASET = \"<the file>\"` in a notebook opens it again with that one assignment; approving it (the quickstart's\napprove(), or exakit describe \\<id> --approve) is what the training and question steps wait for, exploring does not.\nThe rows travel over pyexasol's import on the open connection: no\nhost, user or password here, as everywhere in exakit.nb. Column types come from the file; the date role's column\nbecomes a DATE and a true/false column 0 or 1; a JSON file is an array of records or one record per line, its nested\nvalues kept as JSON text. The table is marked as loaded from the file (its comment holds the file's SHA-256), so\nrunning the cell again loads nothing when the file is unchanged and reloads it when it changed; a table of the same\nname that this did not create is refused unless `replace=True`."],[634,"The descriptor's `source` as written: a dataset id, `file:<path>`, `vs:<alias>` (or a schema_version 1 file's bare alias), or None."],[971,"The descriptor's roles, one per line, as the notebook will use them."],[1213,"The descriptor's roles, one per line, as the notebook will use them."],[636,"The descriptor's version: 1 for a first draft or a shipped file; approving writes the next."],[644,"The digest of the table the descriptor was approved on (its `digest` key, design 2.3: sha256 over the table's name, its columns and types, the row count and an order-independent content hash of the role columns), None until approve computes it."],[40,"The documentation does not open"],[736,"The documentation is a site of plain files the kit ships (`notebook/docs/site` in the kit copy): pages, styles and\na search index, built ahead of time. This module serves that folder from this Python on this computer only\n(the loopback address, a free port) and shows it in a frame under the cell, so reading and searching need no internet, no Node\nand no second install. The server starts on the first call and stops with the kernel."],[365,"The endpoint's address"],[1377,"The exact MCP calls an agent makes to create the preview (no credentials)."],[632,"The external source's alias when the table is in a virtual schema (a live source), else None - what confirm_send and the quickstart ask about."],[775,"The feature view is SQL only - category one-hot over the top-20 values plus OTHER, date -> year / month / ISO day of\nweek / days since the first date, text -> LENGTH, entity -> frequency - so a model that is linear over these columns can\nbe scored by Rust on the very same view (ML-5): TF-IDF stays out of it (the client-side model in explore keeps it);\ntop-k token flags computed in SQL are the deferred next step and are recorded as such in the file. The view is not\ncreated here: the ML quickstart and 01_train create it, with the admin profile."],[776,"The file names a table, columns, SQL and digests, never a host, a user or a password; the kit's secret-grep test\ncovers the folder. A workflow that is active gets one `handoff` line in its log (X-1)."],[1063,"The files `exakit data-load` put into the database, as the kit records them (its load receipts): one row per\ntable, the latest load - \\{table, rows, file, loaded_at}. A kit dataset (sample_datasets) is not a file here."],[915,"The files `exakit data-load` put into the database, as the kit records them (its load receipts): one row per table, the latest load - \\{table, rows, file, loaded_at}."],[451,"The files and folders the notebooks read and write on this computer."],[297,"The first argument is the roles you change, the second the slots. With nothing to change, the saved approval stands."],[1472,"The first card of the quickstart is the kit itself. It has two tabs."],[873,"The first dataset that was loaded, in the order given; says which one is used."],[1209,"The first dataset that was loaded, in the order given; says which one is used."],[415,"The first writes `notebook/docs/out`; the second copies it to `notebook/docs/site` and stamps it with a digest of the sources."],[692,"The five roles of earlier descriptors, read from the slots: \\{role: column}, \\{text: \\[column]}."],[749,"The folder holds the approved column map (`descriptor.yaml`), the schema map when there is one\n(`schema-map.json`), every query the workflow ran with its digest and row count (`queries.sql`), the workflow log\nas it is (`workflow.jsonl`) and a `README.md` that says what the data is, which column map version the numbers rest\non, which questions were approved, which dashboards were published and how to repeat it. Nothing in it is a password:\nthe log is already written without one, and the connection is the kit's."],[730,"The folder that holds the versions of the descriptor `id` (whether or not it exists yet); an id that is not\na dataset id is refused, so no path is built from it."],[855,"The folder that holds the versions of the descriptor `id` (whether or not it exists yet); an id that is not a dataset id is refused, so no path is built from it."],[157,"The groups to compare"],[423,"The guided view"],[435,"The guided view"],[1450,"The guided view"],[216,"The hand-off bundle"],[780,"The handoff as a dict: from a path to the file, from `<id>-v<n>` (that version's file), or from a descriptor\nid (the file with the highest version in the handoffs folder). None there is a FileNotFoundError saying how to\nmake one."],[955,"The handoff as a dict: from a path to the file, from `<id>-v<n>` (that version's file), or from a descriptor id (the file with the highest version in the handoffs folder)."],[774,"The handoff from the Data Scientist to the ML Engineer (DS-3 -> ML-3, design 4): one JSON file that holds everything\n`01_train` needs to train without opening the descriptor - which descriptor version and digest it came from, a digest\nof the data, the feature view built from the roles (as `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` SQL), the label and its positive\nclass, the training SELECT with a reproducible time split, and the input and output schemas. A descriptor without a date\nrole has no time split: the handoff is refused with the fix (`split=\"random\"` for a reproducible hash split, or a\ndate role) - a random split is never silent, and `01_train` refuses one the file does not mark as asked for."],[769,"The handoff from the Data Scientist to the ML Engineer (DS-3 -> ML-3, design 4): one JSON file that holds everything 01_train needs to train without opening the descriptor - which descriptor version and digest it came from, a digest of the data, the feature view built from the roles (as CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW SQL), the label and its positive class, the training SELECT with a reproducible time split, and the input and output schemas."],[777,"The handoff record for `ds` as design 4 shapes it, built now and returned, nothing written: the descriptor's\nid, version, digest (`digest_kind` says whether it is the table digest or the file's) and source; the data\ndigest (`data_digest_kind`); the feature view; the label and its positive class (`label` overrides it);\nthe split (`time` over the date role by default; `split=\"random\"` for a hash split, the only way to get one -\nwithout a date role and without that, a ValueError names the fix; `split.explicit` records the choice) and\n`train_share`; the training SQL; input and output schemas. `workflow_id` defaults to the active workflow's."],[879,"The handoff record for `ds` as design 4 shapes it, built now and returned, nothing written: the descriptor's id, version, digest (`digest_kind` says whether it is the table digest or the file's) and source; the data digest 